<!doctype html>
<html lang="th">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Subnet scan queue | The Watcher</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Run subnet scans in the background and track progress across a subnet range.">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css">
</head>

<body class="queue-page">
    <%-include('components/navigator')%>
    <main class="shell queue-shell">
        <header class="search-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">Background scanner</p>
            <h1>Subnet scan queue</h1>
            <p>Add subnet ranges to the background queue. The scanner handles one job at a time and starts the next job automatically.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="queue-panel" aria-labelledby="queue-form-title">
            <div class="queue-panel-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">New scan range</p>
                    <h2 id="queue-form-title">Set a subnet range</h2>
                </div>
                <span class="queue-mode">ONE SCAN AT A TIME</span>
            </div>
            <p class="queue-help">Enter the first and last subnet prefixes, for example <code>192.168.0</code> to <code>192.168.255</code>. Each /24 is scanned in order (hosts <code>.0–.255</code>). You can add another range while a job is running; it will wait its turn.</p>
            <form id="queue-form" class="queue-form">
                <label>
                    <span>First subnet</span>
                    <input type="text" name="start_range" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="192.168.0" autocomplete="off" required>
                </label>
                <span class="queue-range-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <label>
                    <span>Last subnet</span>
                    <input type="text" name="end_range" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="192.168.255" autocomplete="off" required>
                </label>
                <button id="queue-submit" type="submit">Add to queue</button>
            </form>
            <p id="queue-message" class="queue-message" role="status" aria-live="polite">Enter subnet prefixes with the same first two octets. You can add multiple ranges to the queue.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="queue-panel queue-status-panel" aria-labelledby="queue-status-title">
            <div class="queue-panel-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">Live status</p>
                    <h2 id="queue-status-title">Scan status</h2>
                </div>
                <span id="queue-refresh-status" class="queue-refresh-status">Connecting…</span>
            </div>
            <div id="queue-active" class="queue-active" aria-live="polite">
                <div class="queue-empty-state">No active scan job.</div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="queue-panel" aria-labelledby="queue-history-title">
            <div class="queue-panel-heading">
                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">Recent jobs</p>
                    <h2 id="queue-history-title">Scan history</h2>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div id="queue-history" class="queue-history">
                <div class="queue-empty-state">Loading scan history…</div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
    <script src="/js/scan-queue.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
